    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Spring weather correlated with a documented month-over-month data increase: apprehensions rose from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March along the U.S. border. Yet corroborated long-term statistical context shows year-to-date crossings remain near multi-decade lows under current enforcement policies. Security analysts as trend verifiers provide the quantitative baseline against which this seasonal fluctuation is measured, distinguishing isolated seasonal uptick from systemic shift.",
