    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Data interpreters note the increase in apprehensions from February to March, attributing the shift to a seasonal climatic variable. The quantitative shift in enforcement metric reflects real movement along the southwest border, but the broader enforcement policy outcome remains stable—year-to-date immigration statistics hold near multi-decade lows. This divergence between short-term statistical trend and long-term baseline demands careful observation, not premature conclusion.",
      "source": {
