      "text": "While observers of quantitative patterns track the numerical change at the international boundary, legislative impasse on funding allocation persists among government officials. The political deadlock prevents policy clarity even as experts corroborate the factual landscape—border crosser apprehensions rose seasonally, yet overall crossings remain historically constrained. Fact-based analysis outpaces legislative resolution.",
